# Bounded native observations; not an API or exhaustive coverage proof.
direction: down
classes: {
  start: {style: {fill: "#25364B"; font-color: "#FFFFFF"; bold: true; stroke-width: 3}}
}
Start: "Start here · Signed Koine in an isolated VM\nFresh process and absent consent per case" {class: start}
Directories: "FileManager directory listing\nNames and bounded metadata; no content read"
Ordinary: "Ordinary root / home with exclusions\nNames returned without a prompt"
Protected: "Desktop / Documents / Downloads traversal\nDialog → denial → Cocoa 257"
Applications: "Application-directory listing\nisApplication + Bundle identifier\nNSWorkspace registration lookup"
AppResults: "System applications and Koine found\nRegistered paths returned without a prompt"
Spotlight: "NSMetadataQuery\nLiteral root + filename predicate"
Ambiguous: "Query started; gathering finished\nProtected root prompted, then returned zero\nDisabling indexing retained existing matches"
DesignInput: "Design input\nPrefer bounded name enumeration\nSkip protected traversal before native access\nReport scope and unknown metadata explicitly"
Start -> Directories: "1 · directory cases"
Directories -> Ordinary: "2 · unprotected / excluded scopes"
Directories -> Protected: "2 · explicit experimental protected access"
Start -> Applications: "1 · application cases"
Applications -> AppResults: "2 · inspect candidates"
Start -> Spotlight: "1 · index comparison"
Spotlight -> Ambiguous: "2 · observe results and consent separately"
Ordinary -> DesignInput: "3 · prompt-free candidate route"
Protected -> DesignInput: "3 · cannot traverse on a read"
AppResults -> DesignInput: "3 · discovery within stated roots"
Ambiguous -> DesignInput: "3 · success/count is not an index-health signal"
